<title>SINGAPORE: Transpac injects US$5.4 mln more in Dahe.</title>
<headline>Transpac injects US$5.4 mln more in Dahe.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transpac Industrial Holdings Ltd said on Tuesday it had agreed to invest a further US$5.4 million in Dahe Holding Pte Ltd.</p>
<p>The planned investment, in the form of a convertible loan, would bring Transpac's total stake in Dahe to US$15.4 million, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Dahe is involved in the bottling and sale of spring water in Indonesia and the manufacturing of PET bottles in China.</p>
<p>Transpac said the additional investment would be used for facility improvement and working capital needs of the PET operations.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
